# Which topic page (docs/topics/<name>.md) belongs to which files, for
# scripts/check-topics.py. When a change touches a file here, CI warns
# unless the same change also touches one of its pages.
#
# One rule per line: a path pattern (shell glob, * also matches /) and the
# topic pages, separated by commas; any one of them is enough. The first
# matching rule wins, so specific rules come first. "-" means no topic
# (shared files that many changes touch for their own topic).
# Files in patches/, scripts/, tools/ and config/ that no rule matches get
# a note in the job summary, so this map can be extended.

# Shared by most changes
scripts/build-image.sh                  -
patches/README.md                       -
config/upstream.lock                    ci

# Default patches, by the program they change
patches/base/*RTL8152*                  network,usb
patches/base/*dwc2d*                    usb
patches/base/*usb*                      usb
patches/base/*sdhcid*                   sdcard
patches/base/*sdhostd*                  sdcard
patches/base/*rpi-firmwared*            firmware
patches/base/*getty*                    stability
patches/base/*netstack*                 network
patches/base/*dhcpd*                    network
patches/base/*testnetd*                 network
patches/base/*pcid*                     boot
patches/base/*gpiod*                    firmware
patches/base/*i2cd*                     firmware
patches/base/*spid*                     firmware
patches/base/*                          boot
patches/kernel/*                        stability
patches/relibc/*                        relibc,stability
patches/redoxfs/*                       sdcard
patches/bootloader/*                    boot
patches/fdt/*                           boot

